{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI FAILURE ROOT-CAUSED + FIXED (change 1459 / e63c). Verified-1 cause: src/rebar/types.py is a GENERATED file (python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types, CI drift gate _build-and-test.yml:545) and I hand-edited it. Relocated TERMINAL_STATUSES/is_terminal_status to rebar/reducer/_state.py, exported via rebar.reducer -- all four readers already depend on rebar.reducer, so zero new dependency edges and _ready.py stays dependency-light. types.py regenerated; drift gate clean. Note 1459 had already earned LLM-Review +1 on ps1; only CI failed.\n\nPROCESS FIX: built a local runner for all 16 CI gates ($CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/ci-gates.sh) covering the four generated-artifact drift gates (gen_types/gen_cli_reference/gen_env_registry/gen_mcp_reference --check), the eight source gates, uv lock --check, lint and typecheck. All 16 clean before re-push. This class of Verified-1 should not recur.\n\nStack re-pushed: 1459 ps2 (e63c), 1460 (d064).\n\nDiscovered + filed: dbb2-e329-994d-4c8f -- pre-existing test-isolation bug (tests/unit + tests/scripts/reducer -> rebar_reconciler._loader ModuleNotFoundError), reproduced on pristine origin/main, linked discovered_from e63c."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786070192620503001,"uuid":"c54139df-9b4a-4087-9d44-9a78b518a81a"}